This folder contains registered substrate effects.

## Logic

The design itself is made of transformations that are directly computable. This
means that they can synthesized into programs deterministcally using the AST
mapping for each primitive. 

The actual interaction with reality is not directly computable, these are substrate
level mechanisms that allow the design to intereact with reality. For example, a
websocket connection. On the other hand, there are other substrte level mechanisms
like threads or locks which are also essential for the design to realize its intentions
succesfully. 

So before every behavior, I will let the design call effects that I have registered with
the engine. These effects will contain the mechanisms for the design to actually realize
itself on the substrate. This could be creating a thread, or receiving an input from the
user. 

So in this folder, I am going to let the user register effects that will be synthesized
into the program when substrate level mechanisms are needed. I thought about creating a
new type of behavior called substrate behavior that is interleaved with the design behavior
and I still might go this way but for now, I will start with the design specifying an input
from the user and the engine synthesizing a program that accepts an input from the user
using an effect.